shaderc: writef() formats into a 2 KB stack buffer and, for longer text, formats again into a buffer of exactly the
text's length, so vsnprintf puts its terminating NUL in place of the last character, and that NUL is written out.
It also reused the consumed va_list. The `--depends` file is written this way: a shader whose dependency list passes
2 KB (absolute paths of a deep checkout, a program with many includes) got a depends file ending in NUL instead of its
newline, which cmake/shaderc_cache.py cannot read. The fix sizes the buffer for the terminator and restarts the
argument list. Upstream bgfx has the same code; keep the patch until it is fixed there.

diff --git a/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp b/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
--- a/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
+++ b/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
@@ -460,10 +460,13 @@
 		char* out = temp;
 		int32_t max = sizeof(temp);
 		int32_t len = bx::vsnprintf(out, max, _format, argList);
-		if (len > max)
+		// Storm Engine patch (renderer_bgfx/patches/bgfx-shaderc-long-writef.patch).
+		if (len >= max)
 		{
-			out = (char*)BX_STACK_ALLOC(len);
-			len = bx::vsnprintf(out, len, _format, argList);
+			va_end(argList);
+			va_start(argList, _format);
+			out = (char*)BX_STACK_ALLOC(len + 1);
+			len = bx::vsnprintf(out, len + 1, _format, argList);
 		}
 
 		len = bx::write(_writer, out, len, bx::ErrorAssert{});
